Base: Linux v7.2.10. Built as an out-of-tree module against
linux-armv7-headers 7.2.10-1 (kernel/build.sh). Not tested on hardware.
Do not send upstream as is.

drm/panel: jadard-jd9365da-h3: add the PF1007L photo-frame panel

Add the 10.1 inch 800x1280 MIPI-DSI panel of the EFERCRO PF1007L board
(Humblestead HM-PF1007-BK photo frame, Allwinner A33). The vendor panel
driver name is "yhk_zr789_sq9365_101". The vendor init table starts
with the JD9365DA sequence (E1 93, E2 65, E3 F8, 80 03). The controller ID
was not read from the hardware.

- The init function is generated by kernel/tools/gen_jd9365_init.py from
  the vendor init table (dumps/panel/sq9365_init_sequence.txt). The script
  checks that the code gives the same writes and delays as the table.
- The mode comes from the vendor sys_config.fex [lcd0_para]:
  67 MHz, 800+18+18+18 = 854, 1280+20+4+10 = 1314, 59.71 Hz.
- mode_flags: non-burst video with sync pulses (vendor lcd_dsi_if = 0).

Open points:
- The compatible "yhk,zr789-sq9365-101" is a PLACEHOLDER made from the
  vendor driver name. The panel maker and part number are not known. Neither
  "yhk" nor a real maker is in vendor-prefixes.yaml. The binding
  (jadard,jd9365da-h3.yaml) also needs the new compatible.
- Power sequence fields: set from dumps/panel/power-sequence.md (vendor lcd.ko, read in
  disassembly, not measured). vcioo_to_lp11_delay_ms = 50 and
  lp11_to_reset_delay_ms = 25 give 80 ms from supplies-on to reset-low (the
  common code adds 5 ms), as the vendor does. reset_before_power_off_vcioo =
  true: the vendor sets reset low before it removes the supplies. The 150 ms
  delay at the end of the init function is from the vendor code, not from the
  table. Differences that stay (common code of this driver): one reset pulse
  (vendor: two), 0x28 + 0x10 at power-off (vendor: none), sleep-out and
  display-on with no parameter byte (vendor: one zero parameter).
